        "text": "We have learned fundamental and technical analysis, and you might wonder which is the best to use for you. The answer is each methodology has a different approach that can be suitable at different times. For example, it makes sense to use fundamental analysis if you want to invest and forget over a long period, as technical analysis requires you to regularly check the markets and trade frequently. Fundamental analysis is especially useful with less volatile assets, assets that derive their value mainly from a business or product. Stocks are a good example of this. It's simple to see that the performance of Apple stocks depends on the company's products and their success. You might want to use fundamental analysis to invest in stocks over a long period of time, which is a lower risk method of investing.",
